  "cues": [
    {
      "start": 0.0,
      "end": 4.608,
      "text": "Forty four percent commission sounds like your personal cut, right? Not so fast.",
      "shot": "A giant 44% ticket fills the pink upper stage; a YOU? sticker arrives, then a tilted NOT SO FAST stamp interrupts it. Per-word reveal (dynamic-content-sequencing), centered foreground with striped midground."
    },
    {
      "start": 4.708,
      "end": 10.937,
      "text": "Atomy U S A describes forty four percent of total sales P V as the general commission allocation.",
      "shot": "The ticket becomes a labeled pool container; a 44% fill rises via stat-bars-and-fills while TOTAL SALES PV and GENERAL COMMISSION labels reveal in order. Do not depict 44% of retail price or an individual's sale."
    },
    {
      "start": 11.037,
      "end": 17.587,
      "text": "That pool is distributed among qualified members. It is not a promise that every member gets forty four percent.",
      "shot": "The same pool opens three outlet pipes, drawing paths (svg-path-draw) into three QUALIFIED MEMBER trays; the number of trays is a schematic, not a claim of actual member count. Stack vertically. PERSONAL CUT? stamp crosses out as the sentence resolves."
    },
    {
      "start": 17.687,
      "end": 25.025,
      "text": "Your result depends on the plan's rules. Remember: shared pool, not personal percentage. Save this before you calculate.",
      "shot": "The pipes pull into one diagram card labeled SHARED POOL; scale-swap-transition takes it into a black closing plate with NOT YOUR RATE and a yellow SAVE ticket. Sequential late reveals and final still hold, caption band clear."
    }
  ],
